FINE GROCERIES.
We subscribers would inform their friends and the
public generally that they have just received and
stock of Groceries, suitable for family use, on
consisting in part of the following articles which they
will sell upon reasonable terms.


BEST RIO COFFEE;


New Orleans SUGARS, Loaf & White Crabs;
Lump do.
Young Tyson and Imperial FISH


Sugar House and New Orleans MOLASSES;
TOBACCO, of all kinds;


RICE, best quality; CANDIES, ASSORTED;
LEMONS, ORANGES, FIGS, RAISINS;
Together with stock of FANCY ARTICLES, such as
FISHING TACKLE; COBIES, fancy, and plain;


HAIR OILS; POCKET WALLETS;
And all other things usually kept in a Grocer's
of the kind. CITY & VERSES
Lancaster, April 30 1850.
J. H. MALON, ASHBROOK & CO.
